 ## 2026-08-29
 
+### 1818 — Pi Lifecycle Logs Gain An Explicit Ownership And Retention Boundary
+- DECISION: `tools/agents-infra/internal/infra/pi_config.go` requires positive `max_count`, `max_bytes`, and `max_age_seconds`; there are no numeric defaults or unbounded fallback.
+- FIX: `tools/agents-infra/internal/infra/pi_lifecycle_log_posix.go` retains one deterministic newest-file prefix, exempts only the active file from age pruning, reserves whole JSONL records before writes, and revalidates inode/device/type/mode/link count before unlink.
+- FINDING: Only exact lifecycle names that are mode-0600 single-link regular files are launcher-owned; every other entry is reported as foreign and never pruned.
+- EVIDENCE: Fake-clock/temp-filesystem tests cover active/newest preservation, foreign symlink and wrong-mode preservation, identity replacement refusal, partial-crash deletion, atomic byte refusal, and eight simulated weeks within all configured bounds.
+
+### 1818 — Process-Lifecycle Timing Fixtures Flaked Once And Passed Focused Reruns
+- ANOMALY: One full infra run observed readiness timeout instead of early child exit; one root-package run timed out before the fake tool wrote PID evidence.
+- EVIDENCE: Each exact failing subtest passed immediately with `-count=1`; the later uncached `go test ./... -count=1` exited 0.
+- STATUS: No retained regression evidence; monitor as existing timing sensitivity, not a lifecycle-retention failure.
+
 ### 1646 — Supervision Seconds Duration Overflow Refused
 - REGRESSION: `tools/agents-infra/internal/infra/pi_config.go:424` admitted seconds above 9223372036; later `time.Duration(seconds) * time.Second` overflowed and could make backoff, stable-run, and quarantine timing negative or immediate.
 - FIX: Runtime and shared-supervision seconds now have explicit overflow-safe bounds; doubled lease-stale and handoff sums have effective-duration bounds, broker ordering uses `int64`, and exponential backoff clamps before doubling.
